      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:tou-fd"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-tou-fd-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-tou-fd-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 6 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Voltage level and franchise fee location. FCR-27's three voltage levels and MFF-11's two locations are crossed in one ProfileAlternatives set of six alternatives, because URPX v0.5.1 allows one set per PlanElements and the franchise fee's energy subtotal must include that voltage level's fuel prices. A consumer selects one alternative, for example Secondary Distribution inside city limits. (2) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the non-energy charges' Prices, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (3) Excess Reactive Demand. Where a power factor below 95 percent lagging is indicated, the Company may install metering for reactive demand and bills kVAR above one-third of the measured kW at $0.43 per kVAR. The JSON-LD carries the $0.43 on a calculated MetricInput whose formula is text in its CalculationMethod; a consumer has to compute the excess kVAR, and supplies none for a customer the Company does not meter for it. (4) Business and demand qualifications. The customer must have an annual peak demand of 30 to 250 kW and be a NAICS 722 food service or drinking place, or have been served on TOU-MB-7 at the end of 2019 and on TOU-FD since; accounts were accepted until 6,000 accounts or December 31, 2025. They are stated in the eligibility rule's description, which names only the non-residential customer kind. (5) Minimum Monthly Bill. The sheet sets it at the $123.02 Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, DSM and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every price here is positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (6) Term of Contract. One year: the customer is required to remain on the tariff for twelve months from the contract date, renewed automatically each year unless terminated with 30 days' notice before the anniversary. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
